To save you the agony of dragging out the old AmigaBASIC disk, I've
compiled Mark's Setup program and included it in the archive for you.

It's a bit primitive, but gets you a config file a lot quicker than
doing it in a text editor.

You MUST run this before you run the door, otherwise it won't be able
to find its list of available walls, and I'm not sure what will happen,
but it wouldn't do too much.

The Setup program generates its config file in the current directory,
so make sure you are either CD'd into the door directory itself, or KNOW
what the CD is so you can copy the Config.dat file over to the door
directory.

[PFD 23 Nov 94]

